{"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"text":"The lexicographically first minimum colouring of the simple graph: on each connected","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"component, of all its colourings with its own chromatic number of colours, the one whose","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"colour vector (in ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order) is lexicographically least, Khuller and Vazirani’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"lexicographically first k-colouring (1991) with k = the component’s χ. So within a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"component colours appear in order of first use, colour classes are numbered by their least","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertex, a bipartite component is coloured by its ","type":"text"},{"code":"bipartition()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" sides (left 0), and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"colorCount == chromaticNumber()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Components are not coupled: a bipartite one keeps two","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"colours beside a triangle.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"lexicographicallyFirstMinimumColoring","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14ColoringModule0A0V","text":"Coloring","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/Coloring","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"First fit in index order (the lexicographically first proper colouring of all) when it is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"already optimal. Otherwise each vertex in turn takes the least colour its prefix still","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"extends with (k-colouring’s self-reduction to its decision problem): a Kempe swap of the last","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"colouring found when one avoids the prefix, else DSatur branch and bound over the parts","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"after the prefix that the vertex touches (on sparse components with conflict-directed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"backjumping and restarts). Khuller and Vazirani show the lexicographically first","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"four-colouring of a planar graph is NP-hard to find, though some four-colouring is found in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"polynomial time. It can be far slower than ","type":"text"},{"code":"minimumColoring()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": on random sparse","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"3-colourable graphs with 2n edges it took about 0.2 s at 1,000 vertices, 2.7 s at 2,000 and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"over 100 s at 5,000, where ","type":"text"},{"code":"minimumColoring()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" takes about a millisecond. The search does not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"check for task cancellation.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/graphprotocols\/graph\/lexicographicallyfirstminimumcoloring()"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/lexicographicallyFirstMinimumColoring()","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/Colorin